  "summary": "Recent preprints address mode preservation, quantization-error correction, nonlinear domain design, and quantum interference microscopy.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is control of optical field structure under practical imperfections. Active convolved illumination is reviewed as a framework for preserving optical mode structure through turbulent media. A Fourier-domain response-matrix correction targets quantization errors in binary-encoded Fourier single-pixel imaging. A deterministic poling algorithm for variable sub-coherence-length domains implements arbitrary phase-matching functions while respecting fabrication constraints. A quantum differential interference contrast microscope applies quantum interference to polarization analysis. The new elements are the application of mode preservation, error correction, and quantum interference to specific imaging and nonlinear optics tasks. The listed abstracts emphasize resilience and precision rather than a single shared method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
